From ebe85533812fe47551155a77cdc6e1c0bc825850 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:43:14 -0400
Subject: btrfs: drop the extent maps of the written part of a failed ordered
 extent

From: Tal Zussman <tz2294@columbia.edu>

[ Upstream commit bca2cf55a7331e6b0ff95ad47fc2a7e8ecc7dc74 ]

If a truncated ordered extent fails to complete, the extent maps for the
part that was written are kept while the extent itself is freed below.
A later read can follow them to blocks that have been reallocated.
Drop the maps for the whole range on error.

Fixes: 77cef2ec5484 ("Btrfs: allow partial ordered extent completion")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Tal Zussman <tz2294@columbia.edu>
Signed-off-by: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.com>
[ sashal: Wrapped the btrfs_drop_extent_map_range() call in a local drop_start that resets to start when truncated and ret, since unwritten_start is shared with clear_extent_uptodate() in this tree. ]
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
---
 fs/btrfs/inode.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/btrfs/inode.c b/fs/btrfs/inode.c
index abc834c828519..1c0486591c44f 100644
--- a/fs/btrfs/inode.c
+++ b/fs/btrfs/inode.c
@@ -3434,6 +3434,8 @@ int btrfs_finish_ordered_io(struct btrfs_ordered_extent *ordered_extent)
 
 		/*
 		 * Drop extent maps for the part of the extent we didn't write.
+		 * On error the written part is freed below as well, so drop
+		 * its maps too.
 		 *
 		 * We have an exception here for the free_space_inode, this is
 		 * because when we do btrfs_get_extent() on the free space inode
@@ -3446,9 +3448,15 @@ int btrfs_finish_ordered_io(struct btrfs_ordered_extent *ordered_extent)
 		 * we don't mess with the extent map tree in the NOCOW case, but
 		 * for now simply skip this if we are the free space inode.
 		 */
-		if (!btrfs_is_free_space_inode(inode))
-			btrfs_drop_extent_map_range(inode, unwritten_start,
+		if (!btrfs_is_free_space_inode(inode)) {
+			u64 drop_start = unwritten_start;
+
+			if (truncated && ret)
+				drop_start = start;
+
+			btrfs_drop_extent_map_range(inode, drop_start,
 						    end, false);
+		}
 
 		/*
 		 * If the ordered extent had an IOERR or something else went
-- 
